# shellcheck shell=sh disable=SC2034
# Sourced by /etc/sv/earlyoom/run. Closes the program using the most memory
# before zram fills up and the desktop freezes, the kernel OOM killer acts
# much later. The watchdog notifies through earlyoom-closed.
#   -m 10 -s 10   SIGTERM under 10% available RAM and 10% free swap, both,
#                 SIGKILL under half of them
#   -r 0          no memory reports in the log
#   -p            niceness -20 and oom_score_adj -100: it runs while all waits
# Regexes match /proc/PID/comm, 15 bytes at most. OPTS is split unquoted:
# no spaces (. instead) and no * ? [ in it.
#   --ignore      never closed: the lock screen and what restarts the services
#   --avoid       closed last: the session would go with them
#   --prefer      closed first: browser tabs, Steam's web views, Windows games
OPTS="-m 10 -s 10 -r 0 -p
 -N /usr/local/libexec/earlyoom-closed
 --ignore ^(gtklock|runit|runsvdir|runsv|svlogd|vlogger|socklog|nanoklogd|earlyoom)$
 --avoid ^(g0wm|Xwayland|foot|pipewire|pipewire-pulse|wireplumber|dbus-daemon|elogind-daemon|NetworkManager|wpa_supplicant|dnscrypt-proxy|swayidle|polkitd)$
 --prefer ^(Web.Content|Isolated.Web.Co|steamwebhelper)$|\.exe$"
